      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It is incredibly difficult to accept when a deep personal loss leaves you feeling like your entire existence inside a home has vanished, especially when the reflection that remains seems so foreign to you. That sense of being a \"shell\" often signifies how profoundly grief can disconnect us from our former selves, leaving only the empty space where connections used to be. Please allow yourself the time and space to grieve this transformation without judgment, and consider reaching out to a therapist or support group who understands this specific kind of emotional hollowing out.",
