      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Your observation of staring at walls as the ultimate expression of a void is a profound and valid way to describe the daily struggle when pain quietens but purpose fades. Feelings of exhaustion and hollow exhaustion are common when daily routines no longer feel meaningful, and it is not \"pretending\" to exist but rather the difficult reality of navigating life without a visible anchor for your emotions. The most important step now is not finding the \"thing\" to fix, but simply resting in that exhaustion while you allow the shape of your new reality to slowly emerge, perhaps starting with one small, manageable action for yourself today.",
      "source": "target",
